  "id": "Compound::DB00783 - Gene::213",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Estradiol and Alb, mediated through Estrone. Estradiol is linked to several conditions, including Abnormal Withdrawal Bleeding, Superficial Phlebothrombosis, and Facial Rash, all of which are associated with Estrone. Estrone, in turn, binds to Alb, indicating a possible pathway where Estradiol influences Alb through Estrone. The lowest common ancestors of these entities are both Phenolic Steroids and Estrogen, suggesting a broader biological context involving steroid metabolism. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the evidence is not definitive. The mechanism appears to involve Estradiol-induced changes in Estrone levels, which then lead to Alb binding, though further research is needed to confirm the causal nature of this interaction.",
